            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0543" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/311: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-20T14:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. Your 110, August 19, 5 p.m. While the Foreign Minister’s reply is
                    satisfactory for the purpose of confirming our interpretation, the Department
                    does not intend to publish the exchange of notes. You should so inform Doctor
                    Tobar and add that the Department naturally would not, under such circumstances,
                    wish to have the notes published by the Ecuadoran Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
